\label{main}
Let $K$ be a $n$-dimensional convex body, and let $T_i,\ \{1,2,3,...,n-1\}$ be $n-1$ proper tilings of $K$, each of which contains a tile $L_i$ similar to $K$.\\
If the convex hull of the fixed points $x_{L_i}$ forms a nondegenerate $n-2$-dimensional simplex, then $K$ is a polytope.
